Pass the process wrapper to construct_arguments() explicitly

rules_rust 0.71.0 made construct_arguments() decide via
ctx.executable._process_wrapper whether rustc flags always go into a params
file, see "Always use param files to handle large rustc commands"
(https://github.com/bazelbuild/rules_rust/pull/4038).

That attribute only exists on rules_rust's own rules and aspects, but
construct_arguments() is also reached through the public rust_clippy_action
API, whose docstring demands that it "should not read ctx.attr".  Aspects
defined outside of rules_rust, e.g. aspect_rules_lint's clippy aspect (which
passes its own wrapper around the rules_rust process wrapper), therefore fail
during analysis with:

    Error: No attribute '_process_wrapper' in executable.

rust_clippy_action() already takes the process wrapper as an explicit
argument, it just doesn't hand it on, so let it do that.  This keeps the
params file behavior of PR #4038 for all callers instead of silently
degrading it to the pre-0.71.0 heuristic for those from outside.

diff --git a/rust/private/rustc.bzl b/rust/private/rustc.bzl
--- a/rust/private/rustc.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/rustc.bzl
@@ -984,7 +984,8 @@
         require_explicit_unstable_features = False,
         error_format = None,
         allowed_unstable_rust_features = None,
-        link_std_dylib = False):
+        link_std_dylib = False,
+        process_wrapper = None):
     """Builds an Args object containing common rustc flags
 
     Args:
@@ -1057,6 +1058,9 @@
         error_format (str, optional): Error format to pass to the `--error-format` command line argument. If set to None, uses the "_error_format" entry in `attr`.
         allowed_unstable_rust_features (list, optional): List of unstable Rust language features allowed for this target.
         link_std_dylib (bool): Whether to dynamically link the Rust standard library using `--prefer-dynamic`.
+        process_wrapper (File, optional): The process wrapper which will launch the tool. Defaults to the
+            `_process_wrapper` attribute of the calling rule or aspect, which callers from outside of
+            rules_rust (e.g. via `rust_clippy_action`) don't necessarily have.
 
     Returns:
         tuple: A tuple of the following items
@@ -1194,7 +1198,9 @@
     # Rustc arguments
     rustc_flags = ctx.actions.args()
     rustc_flags.set_param_file_format("multiline")
-    rustc_flags.use_param_file("@%s", use_always = bool(ctx.executable._process_wrapper))
+    if process_wrapper == None:
+        process_wrapper = getattr(ctx.executable, "_process_wrapper", None)
+    rustc_flags.use_param_file("@%s", use_always = bool(process_wrapper))
     rustc_flags.add_all([(crate_info.root, crate_info.root_path)], map_each = _get_crate_root_path)
     rustc_flags.add(crate_info.name, format = "--crate-name=%s")
     rustc_flags.add(crate_info.type, format = "--crate-type=%s")
diff --git a/rust/private/clippy.bzl b/rust/private/clippy.bzl
--- a/rust/private/clippy.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/clippy.bzl
@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@
         file = ctx.file,
         toolchain = toolchain,
         tool_file = clippy_executable,
+        process_wrapper = process_wrapper,
         cc_toolchain = cc_toolchain,
         feature_configuration = feature_configuration,
         crate_info = crate_info,
